  "caption": "Quinn tried a one-handed netball catch and ended up with a puffy, sore finger. Then came the classic advice: just tape it and play on.\n\nMost jammed fingers are sprains that do well with brief protection and early, gentle movement. A fingertip that droops and can't straighten on its own (mallet finger) is different and is worth checking that week.\n\nWhat often helps: buddy-tape simple sprains only, keep the finger moving gently, get stalled movement reviewed, and if you're given a mallet splint, keep it on continuously, even when washing or sleeping.\n\nGet it checked if the tip droops, the finger looks out of shape, there's a wound over a joint, numbness, or lost movement.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
